\centering
\small
\caption{Disagreement-Routed Cascade (DRC) on Mistral-7B ProofWriter ($n{=}600$, $K{=}12$, DeBERTa-large-mnli verifier, $w{=}3$). DRC at $\tau{=}0.7$ achieves 90\% of full-combo accuracy gain while invoking NLI on only 39\% of questions.}
\label{tab:drc}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lccc@{}}
\toprule
Method & Accuracy & NLI Calls & Cost Ratio \\
\midrule
SC only ($\tau{=}0.3$) & 39.33\% & 0/600 & 0\% \\
DRC $\tau{=}0.5$ & 41.50\% & 65/600 & 10.8\% \\
\textbf{DRC $\tau{=}0.7$} & \textbf{45.33\%} & \textbf{233/600} & \textbf{38.8\%} \\
DRC $\tau{=}0.9$ & 45.83\% & 455/600 & 75.8\% \\
Full combo ($w{=}3$) & 46.00\% & 600/600 & 100\% \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

DRC at $\tau{=}0.7$ recovers 90\% of the full-combo accuracy gain ($+6.00$\,pp out of $+6.67$\,pp over SC) while invoking NLI on only 38.8\% of questions. The remaining 61.2\%---where SC traces show high agreement---are correctly resolved by majority vote alone. This confirms that NLI verification is most valuable where SC is uncertain, consistent with Corollary~\ref{cor:capability_gap}: the verifier adds value when the generator's internal consensus is weak.

